## 4. Strict Provenance, Attribution & Authorship Integrity

The rights and permissions granted in Section 3 are strictly conditional upon Your full compliance with the following affirmative requirements:

### 4.1 Preservation of Source Notices
You must retain all original copyright notices, author attributions, legal disclosures, and disclaimer notices in all copies of the Original Code that You distribute in source form.

### 4.2 Mandatory Truthful Attribution
If You distribute the software, a Derivative Work, an operating system distribution, a commercial application, or a physical hardware device incorporating or based on the Original Code, You must include in the accompanying documentation, digital notices file, "About" screen, or packaging a conspicuous and truthful attribution statement substantially equivalent to:

> **"This product contains or is derived from software originally developed as part of the ATOMS OS project (BOS Kernel)."**

### 4.3 Prohibition of False Authorship Claims
You must **NOT**:
1. Falsely claim that You, Your organization, or Your company originally created or engineered the ATOMS OS Original Code;
2. Falsely claim original authorship of the BOS Kernel;
3. Falsely claim original authorship of the BOFS filesystem;
4. Present original ATOMS OS code, architecture, or documentation as Your own independent creation;
5. Conceal or obscure the fact that Your software or product contains or is derived from ATOMS OS.

You may claim authorship solely for Your own original Modifications, additions, or independent components.

### 4.4 Clear Identification of Modifications
If You modify the Original Code, You must ensure that any modified files carry prominent notices stating that the files have been changed, identifying the nature of the changes, and providing the date of modification, so that downstream users can clearly distinguish between the official Original Code and Your modifications.

