ATOMS OS contains, utilizes, and references Third-Party Software developed by external projects and authors. This License applies **solely** to the Original Code authored by Saumya Chaudhari and applicable ATOMS OS contributors.

Third-Party Software remains governed exclusively by its respective upstream licenses, which include without limitation:
* **musl libc**: MIT License (Rich Felker, et al.);
* **LLVM / libc++ / libc++abi**: Apache 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions (LLVM Project Authors);
* **Chromium Core Subsystems**: BSD 3-Clause License (The Chromium Authors);
* **Google V8**: BSD 3-Clause License (The V8 Project Authors);
* **Google Skia**: BSD 3-Clause License (Google Inc. / The Skia Authors);
* **Inter Font Family**: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Rasmus Andersson / The Inter Project Authors);
* **FreeBSD USB & HDA Definitions**: BSD 2-Clause License (The FreeBSD Project, Hans Petter Selasky, Stephane E. Fabie, Alexander Motin, Ariff Abdullah);
* **minimp3 & minimp4**: CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain (Lieven van der Heide, Dmitry Boldyrev);
* **dr_wav & dr_flac**: MIT-0 / Public Domain (David Reid);
* **h264bsd baseline**: Apache 2.0 / MIT (AOSP / PacketVideo / Sam Leitch);
* **FFmpeg CABAC Engine (`h264bsd_cabac.c`)**: GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) Version 2.1 or later (Michael Niedermayer, Loren Merritt, Fabrice Bellard, et al.);
* **libmpv Client**: GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) Version 2.1 or later (mpv developers);
