* **Doom Generic Port**: GNU General Public License (GPL) Version 2 (id Software, Inc. / ozkl — standalone userspace executable).

### 6.2 No Restriction of Upstream Freedoms
Nothing in this License alters, limits, overrides, or restricts any rights, freedoms, or permissions granted to You under any applicable third-party open-source or public license. You must preserve all required upstream copyright notices, license texts, disclaimers, and attribution conditions.

### 6.3 Explicit LGPL v2.1+ and GPL Compliance Carve-Out
1. **LGPL Reverse Engineering Exception**: Where a component of the operating system links or incorporates software governed by the GNU Lesser General Public License (such as `h264bsd_cabac.c`), nothing in this License shall restrict You from modifying or reverse engineering the LGPL-governed portions for debugging such modifications, as permitted under Section 6 of LGPL v2.1.
2. **Userspace GPL Isolation**: Standalone userspace applications licensed under GNU GPL v2 (such as Doom) are independent executables running in user space over standard system calls. Executing such applications does not bring the BOS Kernel or independent subsystems under GPL v2 (constituting mere aggregation under Section 2 of GPL v2). However, distribution of the GPL executable itself remains subject to GPL v2 terms.
3. **Reference Packages**: Uncompiled reference packages residing in the repository (such as `realtek-r8125-dkms`) are reference materials and are not claimed as ATOMS Original Code.

