## 8. Termination & Cure Mechanics

### 8.1 Termination for Material Breach
Your rights and permissions under this License terminate automatically if You materially breach any term, condition, or covenant of this License, specifically including:
1. Intentional removal or concealment of required copyright or provenance notices;
2. False claims of original authorship of the ATOMS OS Original Code, BOS Kernel, or BOFS filesystem;
3. Failure to provide mandatory truthful attribution;
4. Misuse of project brand identities or false claims of official endorsement or certification.

### 8.2 Cure Period for Non-Willful Violations
If Your breach was non-willful and You have not previously received written notice of a breach from the Licensor, Your rights shall be reinstated provisionally upon Your curing the breach within thirty (30) days of receiving notice or becoming aware of the violation, and permanently upon written confirmation from the Licensor.

### 8.3 Survival of Downstream Licenses
Termination of Your rights under this Section shall not terminate the licenses of recipients who received copies, Derivative Works, or products from You under this License, provided that those recipients remain in full compliance.

### 8.4 Scope of Termination
Termination under this Section applies strictly to the permissions granted under this License for the Original Code, and shall not affect or terminate any independent rights granted to You under any third-party license.

